  "limitations": [
    "Production canonical mapping (#227), evidence normalization (#228), credential resolution (#229), current CG-09 policy/consent service (#230), aggregate retry/reconciliation (#231 / EPIC-08) and live reference connectors are not implemented by this slice. Explicit trusted interfaces are required at composition; there is no default authority or raw effect endpoint.",
    "Runtime library and mandatory admitted driving boundary are qualified with injected test authority/mapping/normalization and a synthetic subprocess peer. No installed outbound CLI, live provider, real external mutation or full EPIC-07 acceptance is claimed.",
    "Initial schema profile supports closed objects of string/integer/boolean scalars only; unknown keywords, nested/open objects, decimal/set arguments and incompatible schemas fail closed. Prompt execution, resource-template expansion, tasks, roots, sampling, elicitation and Streamable HTTP are not enabled.",
    "Stdio owns and reaps its direct child. Server-managed descendants remain the server responsibility. Custom transport implementations and trusted callbacks must honor their bounded contracts; blocking callbacks can cause explicit bounded-drain Backpressure.",
    "The runtime never retries or creates budget reservations. Durable reservation reuse, policy revocation/currentness and safe reconciliation are responsibilities of the required application authority; a dispatch record itself grants no authority.",
